 0.8.1 0.8.1 MVP-FOLD-NOTDEPLOYED-1 (2026-10-07, pillar core, agent_issues 2090-2094): a folded MVP component is judged by its fold host unless its own audit row still serves (SYNC, CRON_ONLY or http 200); 0.4.129 deferred to the host only while the old script was absent from the audit or RETIRED_PRESENT, so after cf-ops delete-worker its row read NOT_DEPLOYED (404) and calendar-api, fleet-exec, qnfo-autonomy-scorer, qnfo-paper-indexer and qnfo-paper-reviser filed CHARTER-MVP-DOWN-1 while every host was SYNC. 0.8.0 0.8.0 CI-FEEDBACK-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): when a required check fails on a code-loop pull request, the merge runner reads that job's log and records the failing suites and assertion lines (cmFailureLines, at most 10 lines) in the refusal, so the task's merge_note and its issue say what broke and the next intake retry carries it; before this the note said only "gate=failure" and every retry was blind (PR 750 broke qnfo-ipatent/mechanism.test.mjs, PR 752 changed a value quality.test.mjs:190 pins). merge_note and last_error keep 1200 characters (was 500). 0.7.1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.11 in parity with the charter, which adds decision rule 10 "decide, then record" (RULE-8-RETIRED-1, owner directive 2026-10-06: core prompt rule 8 is deleted); one comment no longer cites rule 8. 0.7.0 CONTROL-PLANE-SELF-MERGE-1 (2026-10-06, transformation lever T1.21, pillar autonomy; owner directive 2026-10-06: more flexibility and autonomy, decide for itself): the stale-PR lane merges a green, quiet session pull request that changes a control-plane worker (CM_DENY) when ops_config control_plane_self_merge is on, the worker has a /health canary (CP_CANARY_WORKERS) and the pull request carries worker.js with its mirror; canonical-deploy.yml canaries /health for the new VERSION and reverts the push on its own (scripts/canary_revert.py, CONTROL-PLANE-CANARY-1), which replaces CONTROL-PLANE-MANUAL-1 (decision (a), human_actions 21, migrations/2