put into a RegExp is escaped whole, and a Markdown table cell (charter, portfolio) escapes a backslash before the pipe. 0.18.0 the merge side of the code loop (owner directive 2026-10-12; issue 2074): GOAL-REVIEW-2 (a goal-review refusal needs two reviewers of different model families; each defect quotes the changed line it is about and is screened against the diff and the file at the head; VERSION, comment and style remarks never refuse; the reviewer reads the whole goal, the diff with long lines shown around their change, and the names the file defines), REFUSAL-REASON-1 + REPAIR-AT-OPEN-1 (a refusal reaches the planner's repair round as ctx.refusal and ctx.lastError, at the open step too), PATCH-REBUILD-1 + MIRROR-FOLLOWS-SOURCE-1 (a change that no longer fits its base is rebuilt from its parked edits or re-proposed, never a dead end; a publish_failed conflict goes back to the orchestrator), MERGE-MULTI-FILE-1 (ctx.paths companions, new files, ctx.x[].edits; ops_config code_merge_multi_file), MERGEABILITY-REQUERY-1 + LANE-TICK-20-1 (the stale-PR lane pre-warms and re-reads a null mergeability before any update-branch, and runs every 20 minutes), PUBLISH-DISPATCH-1 (code-task-publish.yml is dispatched when a task has been ready_to_publish for 10 minutes; ops_config code_publish_dispatch_enabled). 0.17.0 MERGEABILITY-NUDGE-1 + MERGE-REFUSAL-LOG-1 (#2230): a green quiet session PR whose GitHub mergeability stays null (or whose branch is only behind main) gets PUT /pulls/{n}/update-branch pinned to its head and is kept, at most 3 times in 24h (ops_config stale_pr_nudge_enabled), and every non-merge is a branch_hygiene_log row merge-nudge or merge-refused (one per PR, head and reason). STALE-PR-CONFLICT-REPAIR-1 (#2304, carried from PR 910): a quiet PR that conflicts with main gets one deduped high-priority issue with the re-apply procedure (ops_config stale_pr_conflict_repair_enabled). SECRET-COMPARE-1: 32 token comparisons are constant-time; SECURE-ID-1: code task ids come from crypto.getRandomValues. Prior: 0.16.1 PERF-PIN-1 (#2177): ops_config perf_pin:<lever> takes one knob out of the performance loop's search space, so the loop can run again while the owner's q08_max_per_day stays untouched. 0.16.0 CODE-REPAIR-INTASK-1 (owner directive 2026-10-11, deploy success): a goal-review or required-check refusal of an open code-loop PR sends the task back to propose with the defects or failing suite as feedback, on a fresh branch, up to 2 rounds, instead of failing it.  0.13.1: the repair filing also writes cloud_ops_events kind stale-pr-check-repair (the issue-2122 contract proof). 0.13.0 STALE-PR-CHECK-REPAIR-1 (agent_issues 2122): a quiet session PR that is green on every required check but fails only a non-required check (CodeQL) is never merged; the branch sweeper now files one agent_issue per such PR with the failing runs' annotations and a code-task line naming the annotated file, so the finding is fixed instead of the PR being closed unmerged at 24h. */ /* 0.12.2 COST-RUN-RATE-2 (owner request 2026-10-09): fleet_budget ai_spend caps meter the 7-day run rate x 30 from v_cost_run_rate (the daily all-billing cost ledger) instead of a 30-day window; the 30-day figures remain the fallback. */ /* 0.12.1 DETECTOR-CADENCE-1: standing detectors (fm-*, belief-*) are exempt from REMEDIATION-HOLD-1, so failure-mode and belief audits run hourly instead of parking 24 h and closing after 7 days. */ /* 0.12.0 PORTFOLIO-CODE-PUBLISH-1 (#2062, card code-repos-create): the daily portfolio sync creates each staged research-code library's public repository with the fleet token and copies research-code/<name>/ into it (at most 3 per sync, existing files never replaced), then marks the row public. */ /* 0.11.7 CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.14 (DOCTRINE-1, charter section 8 rule 13); no behaviour change. */ /* 0.11.6 CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.13 (ANTIFRAGILE-1, charter section 8 rule 12); no behaviour change. */ /* 0.11.5 QUEUE-SLA-1 (2026-10-08, pillar autonomy,