he gateway, 69 of each 100 Workers AI), reached 7 hours back on its first tick, moved the cursor to the newest row and attributed none of the 4,991 untagged DeepSeek requests of the week (measured 2026-10-07T16:15Z, about $15). Cursor key owner_local_cursor_v2:<gateway>; the v1 key is removed; the event meta reports more and remaining. Also REBASE-BRANCH-ACCEPT-1 (pillar autonomy): cmOpenDecide and cmDecide accept a task's -r<n> rebuilt branch (cmTaskBranch), so a REBASE-REQUEUE-1 rebuild gets its pull request (codeagent-3oa9p0pglnnj-r2 was refused as "not a code-loop branch" at 15:20Z, the path's first live instance); and ISSUE-NOTE-NEWLINE-1: the merge runner's note on a source issue (and the evolve merge note) starts on its own line instead of " | " on the issue's last line, which was the code-anchor: line of 10 open ACT-BRIDGE-1 issues, so their retries ran anchor-less (migrations/2026-10-07-issue-note-newline.sql repairs the open rows). */ /* 0.11.0 OWNER-LOCAL-INGEST-1 (2026-10-07, pillar cost, agent_issues 2080): the hourly tick reads each AI Gateway's request log since a per-gateway cursor and attributes the paid cost: untagged requests (the owner's desktop clients) to ai_spend_owner_local, requests tagged by a fleet worker that keeps no ledger of its own to ai_spend_ledger under that worker; cost_attribution_gap_pct counts both (it read 98 with $21.77 of 7-day DeepSeek cost unattributed), the dashboard gets owner_local_cost_usd_30d. */ /* 0.10.0 SCOPE-SCRIPTS-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy, issue 2101): the merge runner's scope gains kind "script": scripts/*.py and scripts/*.mjs that are not CI gates or guards, suites, deploy primitives or the loop's own runners (CM_SCRIPT_DENY), so a fleet script defect can be a code task instead of session work (issue 2025 sat with a session-task line for scripts/cf_ops_actions.py only because of the scope). A script merges on gate, mirror-guard and comparator (deploy-gate runs the script selftests) and is verified at mer